#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# weierstrass_e2

#% text
# `weierstrass_e2([g2, g3])` gives the root `e2 = weierstrass_p(omega2, [g2, g3])` of `4 t^3 - g2 t - g3`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The half-periods `omega_k` are those of `weierstrass_half_periods` (`omega2 = -omega1 - omega3`).

#% item
# The three roots add up to zero; for `[a, 0]` with `a > 0` and `[0, b]` with `b > 0` the values are closed forms.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
weierstrass_e2([11.0, 7.0])
#% output
#= -0.914213562373095

#% cell
n(weierstrass_e2([5, 1]), 25)
#% output
#= -0.207106781186547524400844362105

#% cell
weierstrass_e2([0.5 + im, 1.0])
#% output
#= -0.2356431391320113 + 0.4246358010727292im

#% cell
weierstrass_e2([1, 0])
#% output
#= 0

#% text
# The roots add up to zero:

#% cell
weierstrass_e1([5.0, 1.0]) + weierstrass_e2([5.0, 1.0]) + weierstrass_e3([5.0, 1.0])
#% output
#= 0.0

